   "install": {
    "title": "Installation",
    "html": "<h5>Linux and Mac</h5>\n<p>Compile and install the extension (supports Postgres 13+)</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-sh\">cd /tmp\ngit clone --branch v0.8.7 https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector.git\ncd pgvector\nmake\nmake install # may need sudo\n</code></pre>\n<p>See the <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#installation-notes---linux-and-mac\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">installation notes</a> if you run into issues</p>\n<p>You can also install it with <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#docker\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Docker</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#homebrew\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#pgxn\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">PGXN</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#apt\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">APT</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#yum\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Yum</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#pkg\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">pkg</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#apk\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">APK</a>, or <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#conda-forge\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">conda-forge</a>, and it comes preinstalled with <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#postgresapp\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Postgres.app</a> and many <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#hosted-postgres\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">hosted providers</a>. There are also instructions for <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/setup-pgvector\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Actions</a>.</p>\n<h5>Windows</h5>\n<p>Ensure <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/building-on-the-command-line?view=msvc-170#download-and-install-the-tools\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">C++ support in Visual Studio</a> is installed and run <code>x64 Native Tools Command Prompt for VS [version]</code> as administrator. Then use <code>nmake</code> to build:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-cmd\">set \"PGROOT=C:\\Program Files\\PostgreSQL\\18\"\ncd %TEMP%\ngit clone --branch v0.8.7 https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector.git\ncd pgvector\nnmake /F Makefile.win\nnmake /F Makefile.win install\n</code></pre>\n<p>See the <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#installation-notes---windows\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">installation notes</a> if you run into issues</p>\n<p>You can also install it with <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#docker\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Docker</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#conda-forge\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">conda-forge</a>.</p>",
